    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_00f97916",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: opens_ice_cream_shop_only_sells_shakes; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image features actor Michael J. Fox in formal attire, juxtaposed with the text 'opens ice cream shop' and 'only sells shakes.' This creates a humorous, ironic, or sarcastic commentary implying that the establishment is deceptive or subpar — perhaps suggesting it's a 'fake' ice cream shop that only offers shakes. While not targeting any specific protected group, the meme's intent is to mock or criticize a business for not meeting expectations, which can be perceived as harmful to the business owner or brand if taken personally. The humor relies on the contrast between the grandeur of the image (Fox in a tuxedo) and the mundane or disappointing product (only shakes), potentially causing reputational harm or negative perception. The meme does not contain abusive, cyberbullying, hateful, misogynistic, or propagandistic elements, but its potential to cause harm lies in its ability to damage a business's reputation through ridicule.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_dfece699"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
