    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_ab27ae9b",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "Michael_J_Fox",
      "label": "Actor Michael J. Fox",
      "description": "Michael J. Fox is a well-known Canadian-American actor, recognized for his roles in popular films and TV shows, including 'Back to the Future' and 'Family Ties'. His public image is often associated with charm, intelligence, and a certain level of sophistication, especially when seen in formal attire. The meme leverages his recognizable persona to create irony — juxtaposing his polished, high-status appearance with the mundane or disappointing product (shakes) he is humorously implied to be associated with. This contrast is central to the meme’s humor and requires knowledge of his public identity and career to be fully understood.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_dfece699"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_9e700853",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "text_chunk_1",
      "label": "Textual Material: 'opens ice cream shop'",
      "description": "The phrase 'opens ice cream shop' is a common trope in memes and jokes, implying a business venture that is expected to offer a specific, popular product (ice cream). This phrase sets up an expectation that is then subverted by the second text. The humor relies on the audience understanding that 'ice cream shop' is a specific type of establishment, and the contrast with 'only sells shakes' is only funny if the viewer knows that ice cream shops typically offer more than just shakes. This requires cultural knowledge of common business expectations and food industry norms.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_dfece699"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_c3c6686a",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "text_chunk_2",
      "label": "Textual Material: 'only sells shakes'",
      "description": "The phrase 'only sells shakes' is a punchline that subverts the expectation set by 'ice cream shop'. It implies deception or a lack of quality, suggesting the business is misleading or subpar. This requires knowledge of consumer expectations and the common understanding that ice cream shops offer a variety of products, not just shakes. The humor is derived from the contrast between the grandeur of the image and the disappointing product, which is only funny if the viewer understands the implied critique of the business.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_dfece699"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_5a760aca",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "formal_event_attire",
      "label": "Formal Event Attire",
      "description": "The image shows Michael J. Fox in a tuxedo, which is formal attire typically worn at high-profile events, galas, or red carpet appearances. This attire is associated with sophistication, celebration, and high status. The meme uses this visual contrast — the grandeur of formal wear juxtaposed with the mundane product — to create irony. The humor relies on the audience understanding the cultural significance of formal attire and how it contrasts with the implied low-quality or deceptive nature of the business.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_dfece699"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_f87e0b0b",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "ice_cream_shop",
      "label": "Ice Cream Shop",
      "description": "An ice cream shop is a type of retail establishment that sells ice cream and related products. The term 'ice cream shop' is culturally understood to imply a variety of offerings, including ice cream cones, sundaes, and shakes. The meme relies on this common understanding to create its humor — the expectation that an ice cream shop offers more than just shakes. This requires knowledge of common business types and consumer expectations.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_dfece699"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_fe4455b5",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "shake",
      "label": "Shake",
      "description": "A shake is a blended beverage, often made with ice cream, milk, or other ingredients. While shakes are a common product in ice cream shops, they are not typically the sole offering. The meme uses the phrase 'only sells shakes' to imply that the business is deceptive or subpar, which requires knowledge of what is typically offered in an ice cream shop and the cultural understanding that shakes are not the primary product.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_dfece699"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_642f558c",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "meme_structure",
      "label": "Meme Structure: Juxtaposition and Irony",
      "description": "The meme uses a common structure in internet humor: juxtaposing a high-status or glamorous image with a mundane or disappointing text. This structure relies on the audience understanding the contrast between the visual and textual elements to derive humor. The humor is derived from the irony of the situation — the grandeur of the image (Michael J. Fox in a tuxedo) contrasted with the mundane product (shakes). This requires knowledge of meme conventions and the cultural understanding of irony.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_dfece699"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_cd47aeff",
      "@type": "EmotionExpression",
      "instance_name": "irony",
      "label": "ironic expression",
      "description": "The emotion expressed is irony, derived from the humorous contrast between Michael J. Fox's formal, high-status appearance (tuxedo) and the mundane, disappointing product implied by the text ('only sells shakes'). The visual grandeur juxtaposed with the textual punchline creates a sarcastic commentary on the business's perceived deception or subpar offerings.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_dfece699"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_72c87ad3",
      "@type": "AnalogicalMapping",
      "instance_name": "mapping_1",
      "label": "Michael J. Fox is mapped as the owner of the ice cream shop",
      "description": "The text 'opens ice cream shop' is mapped onto Michael J. Fox, who is visually depicted in formal attire. The meme implies that he is the person who opened the establishment, creating an analogical mapping where the actor is projected as the business owner. This mapping relies on the juxtaposition of his high-status appearance with the mundane nature of the business, enhancing the irony.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_dfece699"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_42a16229",
      "@type": "SemioticProjection",
      "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
      "label": "User projected onto the textual material implying a deceptive business venture",
      "description": "The user is projected onto the textual material 'only sells shakes' as the target of the meme's ironic commentary. The user imagines themselves as the consumer or observer who is deceived by the business's misleading name ('ice cream shop') and disappointing product offering ('only sells shakes'). This projection is implicit, as the meme does not use explicit deictic pronouns like 'you' or 'me', but the humor and critique are directed at the user's perception of the business's dishonesty or subpar quality. The user is thus projected onto the textual punchline, which represents the core of the meme's ironic message.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_dfece699"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_2a957b67",
      "@type": "ToxicityAssessment",
      "instance_name": "toxicity_1",
      "label": "Harmful",
      "description": "The meme humorously implies that Michael J. Fox’s ice cream shop is deceptive or subpar by only selling shakes, which can cause reputational harm to the business owner or brand if taken personally. The humor relies on the contrast between the grandeur of the image and the mundane product, potentially damaging a business’s reputation through ridicule.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_dfece699"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_8ffc3839",
      "@type": "TargetCommunity",
      "instance_name": "audience_id",
      "label": "general internet meme audience",
      "description": "The meme is designed for a broad, general internet audience familiar with pop culture, internet humor conventions, and the actor Michael J. Fox. The humor relies on cultural knowledge of ice cream shops offering more than just shakes, the irony of juxtaposing a high-status image (Michael J. Fox in a tuxedo) with a mundane product (shakes), and the common meme structure of subverting expectations. The target audience understands these references and finds the contrast humorous, even if it implies a critique of the business owner.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_dfece699"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    }
